          "type": "thinking",
          "thinking": "Now I have a clear understanding of the `cmd_check_anchors` function. I need to:\n\n1. Track the Sigstore attestation time (`t`) for each range head (the `hi` in ranges)\n2. Track the OTS proof status (the `t` returned by `check_ots`) for each range head\n3. After processing all anchors, if `--max-pending-hours` is set, check each range head:\n   - If the OTS proof is pending (None) and the attestation time is more than H hours ago, add to bad list\n\nLet me modify the function. I need to:\n- Store the attestation time for each range head when processing sigstore anchors\n- Store the OTS proof status for each seq when processing ots anchors\n- After the loop that checks for missing OTS proofs, add the new check for pending proofs older than max-pending-hours\n\nLet me write the modified function.",
