          "type": "text",
          "text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've added the `--max-pending-hours H` option to `python3 record/record.py check-anchors` as required.\n\n### Changes made to `/workspace/record/record.py`:\n\n1. **Added the command-line argument** (line ~621):\n   ```python\n   p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, metavar=\"H\",\n                  help=\"if a range head's OTS proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation is more than H hours old, exit 1\")\n   ```\n\n2. **Modified `cmd_check_anchors` function** to:\n   - Track Sigstore attestation times for each range head (`attestation_times` dict)\n   - Track OTS proof status for each seq (`ots_status` dict - block time or `None` if pending)\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is set, iterate through range heads and check:\n     - If OTS proof is pending (`ots_time is None`) AND attestation time exists\n     - Calculate age in hours since attestation\n     - If age > H hours, add error: `anchors/NNNNNN.ots: still pending N h`\n\n### Behavior:\n- **Without `--max-pending-hours`**: Unchanged - pending proofs accepted (exit 0)\n- **With `--max-pending-hours H`**: \n  - Pending proof with attestation > H hours ago → exit 1, prints `still pending N h` to stderr\n  - Pending proof with attestation ≤ H hours ago → exit 0\n  - Confirmed OTS proof → never affected by this check (exit 0)\n\n### Testing:\n- All 21 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` pass\n- Manual verification confirms the new functionality works correctly for various scenarios"
